    "task": "text-ranking",
    "description": "A large Chinese-and-English cross-encoder running locally with Transformers.js. It scores paired queries and candidate passages and returns ranked documents with original indices, raw logits and optional sigmoid scores.",
    "intendedUses": [
      "Rerank a bounded candidate set from lexical or embedding retrieval.",
      "Chinese/English search and RAG ranking prototypes.",
      "Browser cross-encoder performance comparison."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Every query-document pair requires inference; this is not a whole-corpus embedding index.",
      "Even INT8 weights exceed 561 MB; FP32 uses external weights exceeding 2.2 GB and may hit browser memory or cache limits.",
      "Scores are relative relevance signals, not calibrated probabilities, factuality checks or safety judgments.",
      "Long paired inputs are truncated at max_length and can lose important evidence.",
      "Accuracy can degrade for unsupported languages, specialized domains, adversarial input and missing context.",
      "Training biases and incorrect rankings require review before consequential decisions."
    ]
  },
